{
  "name": "midnight-dispatch",
  "vibe": "A late-night newsroom cut into a 16:9 broadcast slate: near-black ink and deep midnight navy grounds, bone-white Big Shoulders Display headlines snapping in on the beat, one hot amber (#ffb020) reserved for the single thing that matters and an anchor blue (#0d77e7) doing the wiring — chip outlines, card frames, tile rules. The world is a faint 40-line scanline field over a blue signal bloom with one slow amber beam sweep, so the frame breathes like a monitor rather than a slideshow. Hard cuts, no crossfades, no shadows, every headline on one line. Built for editorial explainers, product bulletins, market recaps, tech news and anything that wants to sound like it is going out live at 11pm.",
  "orientation": "landscape",
  "category": "Editorial",
